<title>DUBAI: Saudi Aramco changes bunker fuel prices.</title>
<headline>Saudi Aramco changes bunker fuel prices.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Aramco has raised A-960 bunker fuel from Ras Tanura and Dammam by $3 a tonne to $105 ($16.12 a barrel) with effect March 6, the company said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A-960 from Jeddah and Yanbu was cut by $4 a tonne to $98.</p>
<p>A-888 bunker diesel from Gulf ports remained the same at $212 a tonne and that from Red Sea ports was cut by $5 to $188 a tonne.</p>
</text>
